    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A curve has equation = ,      x∈ , x &gt; y x ln x 0 . Find the exact coordinates of the two points on the curve which have gradient 3 2 . ( ) 9\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The real curve starts at x = 1; on x &gt; 1, [M1] write y = x(ln x)1/2; differentiating yields 1 · (ln x)1/2 + x · 1 2(ln x)−1/2(1/x). Thus the product and chain rules give √ √ y′ = ln x + 1/(2 ln x). [A1] √ The right derivative at 1 is unbounded: [A1] Set s = ln x &gt; 0. Then s + 1/(2s) = 3/2 [A1] gives 2s2 + 1 = 3s, 2s2 −3s + 1 = 0, hence (2s −1)(s −1) = 0. [A1] The two cases give ln x = s2 = 1/4 or 1. For s = 1/2, x = e1/4 [A1] and y = 1 2e1/4; [A1] for s = 1, x = y = e. [A1] The two points are (e1/4, e1/4/2), (e, e) . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
