    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Let F(x) = x2 −2x−1/2 −3x−2. √ It is continuous on [1, 2], with F(1) = −4 &lt; 0 and F(2) = 13/4 − 2 &gt; 0. [B1] Therefore the root lies between 1 and 2 . [A1] (b) F ′(x) = 2x + x−3/2 + 6x−3. [B1] [A1] Substituting into xn+1 = xn −F(xn)/F ′(xn), [M1] the numerator after multiplication by x3 n is n + x3/2 n −2x5/2 xn(2x4 + 6) −(x5 −3xn). n n n + x5/2 n + 2x5/2 Expand to obtain 2x5 + 6xn −x5 + 3xn. n n Thus combining the fractions and multiplying top and bottom by x3 n gives n + 3x5/2 xn+1 = x5 + 9xn n . [M1] [A1] 2x4n + x3/2 + 6 n\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(c) Starting at 1.5 gives 1.6345944846, 1.6375654056, 1.6375662279, . . .. The fourth and fifth iterates agree at 1.637566228 to nine decimal places: Hence α = 1.63756623 to eight decimal places: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:502.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 8 marks.</p>"
