      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Write (2 −x)−3 = 2−3(1 −x/2)−3. In the binomial formula put z = −x/2: the successive coefficients of z, z2, z3 are −3, (−3)(−4)/2!, (−3)(−4)(−5)/3!. For |x| &lt; 2, (2 −x)−3 = 1  1 + 3 2x + 3 2x2 + 5 4x3 + O(x4)  . [B1] [A1] 8 The two product rows are = 1 8A + 3 16Ax + 3 16Ax2 + 5 32Ax3 + O(x4) +1 8Bx + 3 16Bx2 + 3 16Bx3 + O(x4) Multiplying by A + Bx, the constant coefficient 1/4 gives A = 2, [M1] [A1] and the missing linear term gives 3A/2 + B = 0, [A1] so B = −3. [A1] Then\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"C = (3A/2 + 3B/2)/8 [A1] = −3/16 and D = (5A/4 + 3B/2)/8 = −1/4 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
