    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-u/q12",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A sequence  1t , 2t , 3t , 4t , 5t , … is given by t + = at + 3 n + 2 ,   t ∈ ,  1 t = −, 2 n 1 n where a is a non zero constant. 3  3 ( ) a) Given that ( r + t ) = 12 , determine the possible values of a . 7 r r = 1 31  b) Evaluate ( t − at ) . ( ) 5 r + 1 r r = 8\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With t1 = −2, substitute into the recurrence: t2 = at1 + 3 × 1 + 2 = a(−2) + 3 + 2 = 5 −2a t3 = at2 + 3 × 2 + 2 = a(5 −2a) + 6 + 2 = 8 + 5a −2a2 The recurrence gives t2 = 5 −2a, t3 = 8 + 5a −2a2. [M1] [A1] Expand the cube sum as 3 X (tr + r3) = (t1 + 13) + (t2 + 23) + (t3 + 33) r=1 = t1 + 1 + t2 + 8 + t3 + 27 = t1 + t2 + t3 + 36 = −2 + (5 −2a) + (8 + 5a −2a2) + 36 = −2a2 + 3a + 47\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-u/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus the sum is 36 + t1 + t2 + t3 = 47 + 3a −2a2. [M1] [A1] Equating it to 12 gives (a −5)(2a + 7) = 0, [M1] so a = 5 or −7/2 . [M1] [A1] (b) By the recurrence tr+1 −atr = (atr + 3r + 2) −atr. Each summand is 3r + 2. [B1] [A1] These 24 terms run from 26 to 95 in steps of 3; their sum is 12(26 + 95) = 1452 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
